<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:37:50 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>在科罗拉多州首届肥胖土拨鼠周期间为最矮胖的高山啮齿动物投票</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/cast-your-vote-for-the-chunkiest-alpine-rodent-during-colorados-first-ever-fat-marmot-week-180989395/</link><description>首届比赛让八只黄腹土拨鼠正面交锋，同时揭示了它们季节性体重增加和高海拔生存背后的科学原理</description><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 19:33:40 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/cast-your-vote-for-the-chunkiest-alpine-rodent-during-colorados-first-ever-fat-marmot-week-180989395/</guid></item><item><title>马萨诸塞州一座新雕像纪念《白鲸》作者赫尔曼·梅尔维尔，他的捕鲸冒险就是从这里开始的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-statue-honors-moby-dick-author-herman-melville-in-the-massachusetts-city-where-his-whaling-adventures-began-180989388/</link><description>这件 7.5 英尺高的青铜艺术品矗立在历史悠久的新贝德福德市中心，这座 19 世纪的捕鲸港为作者在 1851 年创作著名小说提供了灵感</description><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 17:57:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-statue-honors-moby-dick-author-herman-melville-in-the-massachusetts-city-where-his-whaling-adventures-began-180989388/</guid></item><item><title>在苏格兰的一个神秘石结构内发现了一具人类骨骼。考古学家仍然不知道为什么它被埋在那里</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/human-skeleton-found-inside-mysterious-stone-structure-in-scotland-archaeologists-still-dont-know-why-it-was-buried-there-180989391/</link><description>这种不寻常的结构是用合适的石头和类似粘土的材料建造的，可能有助于保留液体，这种不寻常的结构让研究人员寻找解释</description><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 17:51:55 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/human-skeleton-found-inside-mysterious-stone-structure-in-scotland-archaeologists-still-dont-know-why-it-was-buried-there-180989391/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，这些小鼩鼱会长出更大的鼻子并缩小大脑以度过严冬</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-tiny-shrews-grow-bigger-snouts-and-shrink-their-brains-to-survive-harsh-winters-study-suggests-180989369/</link><description>科学家们早就知道，一些小型哺乳动物的大脑在寒冷的月份会缩小，并在春天重新生长。来自日本北海道的长爪鼩鼱似乎遵循这种模式，而令人惊讶的是它们的鼻子却相反</description><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:36:12 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-tiny-shrews-grow-bigger-snouts-and-shrink-their-brains-to-survive-harsh-winters-study-suggests-180989369/</guid></item><item><title>中国的这种岩画近2000年来一直保持鲜红色。如何？秘密成分可能是血</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-rock-art-in-china-has-remained-bright-red-for-nearly-2000-years-how-the-secret-ingredient-might-be-blood-180989389/</link><description>一项新的研究提供了关于洛越人如何在现在的中国南方创作岩画的线索。几个世纪以来，这些壁画都足够耐用，可以承受雨水、高温、风和湿度</description><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-rock-art-in-china-has-remained-bright-red-for-nearly-2000-years-how-the-secret-ingredient-might-be-blood-180989389/</guid></item><item><title>在法国，夏季的酷暑热浪正在对那些为克劳德·莫奈最受喜爱的画作提供灵感的花朵造成影响</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-france-brutal-summer-heat-waves-taking-toll-on-flowers-that-inspired-claude-monet-most-beloved-paintings-180989384/</link><description>今年夏天，法国正面临创纪录的 52 天热浪，艺术家家和花园里色彩缤纷的旱金莲受到了特别严重的打击。</description><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 20:06:03 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-france-brutal-summer-heat-waves-taking-toll-on-flowers-that-inspired-claude-monet-most-beloved-paintings-180989384/</guid></item><item><title>“独一无二”的水母博物馆安全地在玻璃后面展示令人惊叹的海荨麻，令游客惊叹不已</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/only-one-of-its-kind-jellyfish-museum-opens-in-florida-astounds-visitors-awe-inspiring-displays-nettles-safely-behind-glass-180989381/</link><description>该博物馆于春季开放，由两位逃离俄罗斯-乌克兰战争的水族馆专家创办</description><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 17:55:33 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/only-one-of-its-kind-jellyfish-museum-opens-in-florida-astounds-visitors-awe-inspiring-displays-nettles-safely-behind-glass-180989381/</guid></item><item><title>这条 15 英尺长的蟒蛇是已知的第一条接受电化学疗法治疗癌症的蛇。现在，她正式摆脱了这种疾病</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-15-foot-python-is-the-first-known-snake-to-receive-electrochemotherapy-for-cancer-now-shes-officially-free-of-the-disease-180989385/</link><description>这种开创性的治疗方法使传统化疗药物更容易渗透癌细胞。手术后，这只名叫朱迪·福斯特的爬行动物很快康复了</description><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 17:31:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-15-foot-python-is-the-first-known-snake-to-receive-electrochemotherapy-for-cancer-now-shes-officially-free-of-the-disease-180989385/</guid></item><item><title>自二战以来对公众关闭的伦敦自然历史博物馆的“隐藏”画廊再次向公众开放</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/closed-to-public-since-wwii-hidden-gallery-at-london-natural-history-museum-opens-doors-once-again-180989380/</link><description>重新开放的“自然与我们”展览将展出数十件物品，包括动物骨骼、新石器时代工具和流行文化纪念品等</description><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 17:18:09 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/closed-to-public-since-wwii-hidden-gallery-at-london-natural-history-museum-opens-doors-once-again-180989380/</guid></item><item><title>几个世纪前，欧洲饱受持续洪涝之苦，短短三年内发生16起重大事件导致数千人死亡</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/centuries-ago-europeans-plagued-constant-flooding-16-major-events-killed-thousands-over-course-three-years-180989378/</link><description>当研究人员寻找有关传说中的马格达莱纳洪水的信息时，他们惊讶地发现，这只是 1340 年代初蹂躏该地区的众多极端天气事件之一</description><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 16:43:17 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/centuries-ago-europeans-plagued-constant-flooding-16-major-events-killed-thousands-over-course-three-years-180989378/</guid></item><item><title>科学家利用人工智能设计新病毒。该技术可能为医学带来福音，但专家担心有害病原体</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-used-ai-too-design-new-viruses-the-technology-could-be-a-boon-for-medicine-but-experts-worry-about-harmful-pathogens-180989336/</link><description>这些发现代表了第一个基因组或完整的基因指导书，完全由生成人工智能设计产生的病毒只攻击细菌，这有一天可能有助于克服抗生素耐药微生物的问题</description><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 16:08:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-used-ai-too-design-new-viruses-the-technology-could-be-a-boon-for-medicine-but-experts-worry-about-harmful-pathogens-180989336/</guid></item><item><title>制药商表示，一种新的个性化癌症疫苗可以防止皮肤癌复发</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/new-personalized-cancer-vaccine-could-keep-skin-cancer-from-coming-back-drugmakers-say-180989382/</link><description>Moderna 和默克公司本周宣布的结果可能为针对个体肿瘤的新一代治疗方法铺平道路</description><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 18:16:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/new-personalized-cancer-vaccine-could-keep-skin-cancer-from-coming-back-drugmakers-say-180989382/</guid></item><item><title>沉船猎人发现了一艘英国驱逐舰的废墟，该驱逐舰在 118 年前的一次悲惨和平时期事故中裂成两半</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/shipwreck-hunters-discover-the-ruins-of-a-british-destroyer-that-split-in-half-during-a-tragic-peacetime-accident-118-years-ago-180989379/</link><description>与一艘万吨级巡洋舰相撞几分钟后，英国皇家海军“虎”号沉入英吉利海峡底部。过去四年来，潜水员和历史学家一直在寻找这艘皇家海军船只</description><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 18:04:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/shipwreck-hunters-discover-the-ruins-of-a-british-destroyer-that-split-in-half-during-a-tragic-peacetime-accident-118-years-ago-180989379/</guid></item><item><title>科学家对狗进行了核磁共振成像，结果发现它们非常擅长区分人类情绪，甚至是一些负面情绪</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-gave-dogs-mris-and-learned-that-theyre-surprisingly-good-at-distinguishing-between-human-emotions-even-some-negative-ones-180989329/</link><description>最近的一项研究发现，人类最好的朋友以不同的方式处理积极和消极的人类情绪，并且可以区分恐惧的面孔和表现出悲伤或愤怒的面孔</description><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:58:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-gave-dogs-mris-and-learned-that-theyre-surprisingly-good-at-distinguishing-between-human-emotions-even-some-negative-ones-180989329/</guid></item><item><title>一只“极其罕见”的半雄半雌鸟暂时在芝加哥郊外定居</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-extremely-rare-half-male-half-female-bird-temporarily-took-up-residence-outside-of-chicago-180989377/</link><description>长相不寻常的bobolink是所谓的双侧雌雄同体动物。这只鸟的行为像雄性，最终追求配偶并抚养雏鸟</description><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-extremely-rare-half-male-half-female-bird-temporarily-took-up-residence-outside-of-chicago-180989377/</guid></item><item><title>这些“极其罕见”的 17 世纪绘画保存得令人惊讶。现在它们是近一个世纪以来首次展出</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/extremely-rare-artworks-from-17th-century-drawing-book-were-astonishingly-well-preserved-now-they-are-on-display-for-first-time-in-nearly-century-180989374/</link><description>阿姆斯特丹国家博物馆获得了这本图画书，其中的作品出自 17 世纪荷兰著名画家 Rombout Uylenburgh 之手，他的遗产后来陷入了默默无闻</description><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 12:00:40 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/extremely-rare-artworks-from-17th-century-drawing-book-were-astonishingly-well-preserved-now-they-are-on-display-for-first-time-in-nearly-century-180989374/</guid></item><item><title>美国宇航局资助的救援坠落太空望远镜的任务正式以失败告终</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nasa-funded-mission-to-rescue-a-falling-space-telescope-officially-ends-in-failure-180989376/</link><description>商业 LINK 航天器本应为 NASA 的雨燕天文台提供动力，将其推入更高的轨道以延长其寿命。但推出后，LINK 遇到了一些问题。雨燕预计将在今年年底重新进入地球大气层并燃烧殆尽</description><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:35:40 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nasa-funded-mission-to-rescue-a-falling-space-telescope-officially-ends-in-failure-180989376/</guid></item><item><title>贝叶挂毯应该如何结束？一项新的竞赛邀请孩子们重新想象其缺失的最终面板</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-should-the-bayeux-tapestry-end-new-a-competition-invites-childresn-to-reimagine-its-missing-final-panel-180989366/</link><description>一些历史学家认为这幅 230 英尺长的艺术品缺少最后一块面板，该面板可能曾经描绘过征服者威廉的加冕典礼。当挂毯在伦敦展出时，学生们将起草自己的结局</description><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:50:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-should-the-bayeux-tapestry-end-new-a-competition-invites-childresn-to-reimagine-its-missing-final-panel-180989366/</guid></item><item><title>独角鲸具有标志性的直螺旋獠牙。科学家刚刚揭开了一些引人注目的结构秘密</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/narwhals-sport-iconic-straight-spiraled-tusks-scientists-just-uncovered-some-of-the-eye-catching-features-structural-secrets-180989368/</link><description>北极鲸是唯一已知的长着直牙的动物，而且牙总是向左扭曲。新研究表明，内层向右扭曲，相反的螺旋提供强度并帮助象牙笔直生长</description><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:11:05 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/narwhals-sport-iconic-straight-spiraled-tusks-scientists-just-uncovered-some-of-the-eye-catching-features-structural-secrets-180989368/</guid></item><item><title>奥地利的建筑工程在足球场下发现了罗马时代的万人坑。新研究表明男性的敌人瞄准了他们的“敏感区域”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/construction-in-austria-revealed-roman-era-mass-grave-beneath-soccer-field-new-research-suggests-that-the-mens-enemies-targeted-their-sensitive-areas-180989372/</link><description>没有书面记录提及在这些人死亡时维也纳这一特定地区发生过战斗。但他们受伤的残酷性质，特别是骨盆区域，表明这些人死在战场上</description><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:06:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/construction-in-austria-revealed-roman-era-mass-grave-beneath-soccer-field-new-research-suggests-that-the-mens-enemies-targeted-their-sensitive-areas-180989372/</guid></item></channel></rss>